{
 "section_summary": "The section opens in the middle of a numbered digest of wartime reports about Japanese administration and economic activity across the Philippines, the Netherlands East Indies, Malaya, North Borneo, Burma, Thailand, and French Indochina. It then contains a telegram and paraphrase reporting Chinese intelligence estimates of synthetic fuel production and North Borneo oil wells, followed by correspondence transmitting an economic appraisal. The appraisal assesses Japan’s shortages, shipping, wartime administration, and policy in occupied China; it continues beyond page 182.",
